# PRD D-16 and roadmap section 30: Conventional Commits, validated per message.
#
# --no-install so a missing package fails loudly instead of npx quietly
# downloading it, which would hide a broken install behind a slow commit.
#
# git revert generates "Revert ..." which this config rejects. That is the
# intended behaviour; pass --no-verify to record the revert as git wrote it.
#
# @see docs/DECISIONS.md D-28
npx --no-install commitlint --edit "$1"
